      {
        "text": "Daniel Biss has been the mayor of Evanston, Illinois, since 2021. He previously served in the Illinois State Senate from 2013 to 2019 and in the Illinois House of Representatives from 2011 to 2013. Before entering politics, he was a mathematics professor at the University of Chicago.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Daniel Biss has been the mayor of Evanston, Illinois, since 2021.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He previously served in the Illinois State Senate from 2013 to 2019 and in the Illinois House of Representatives from 2011 to 2013.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "Before entering politics, he was a mathematics professor at the University of Chicago.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Biss supports Medicare for All and has proposed lowering the Medicare eligibility age from 65 to 55 as a first step. He has called for abolishing U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement as it currently exists. At a candidate debate, he called for stronger enforcement of antitrust laws to reduce the power of large corporations to raise prices and cut wages. He favors a moratorium on new data centers, partly to slow the growth of artificial intelligence, which he considers a serious threat. He supports a two-state solution and has called for the U.S. to enact the Block the Bombs Act and recognize a Palestinian state. In a candidate questionnaire, he said he would introduce legislation to mandate minimum staffing levels for federal offices that enforce disability rights.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4, 5],
        "sentences": [
